  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Venture an Idea Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Serbia):  USAID&apos;s Venture an Idea Activity focuses on building the entrepreneurial mindset of younger generations and accelerating Serbia&apos;s innovation-driven development. There have been important developments both in terms of Serbian government reforms to spur on innovation but also increased investment from the private sector. However, success stories of Serbia&apos;s innovative businesses in the global context remain outliers. This activity looks at younger generations to increase the number of entrepreneurs and/or startup founders. The activity has four main objectives: 1) to embed and develop an entrepreneurial mindset in younger generations to start their own businesses, develop technology and build innovative business models; 2) to pilot/demonstrate co-creation of innovative products and services in order to increase their commercialization and boost creativity within targeted groups; 3) to support selected startups to increase their global reach; and 4) to improve connections between business and academia. This activity supports the USG&apos;s priority to grow economic opportunities and prosperity. It supports ICS Mission Objective 2.1 &quot;Broad-Based, Inclusive, and Sustainable Economic Growth Accelerated, Including Through Improved Access to U.S. and European Finance and an Improved Ecosystem for the Knowledge-Based Economy.&quot; In line with USAID&apos;s pre-obligation requirement standards, the Mission verifies that all assistance activities do not have an adverse economic effect on the United States.</narrative>
  </description>
